DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       ccaattggeettss() reads the message _m_e_s_s_a_g_e___n_u_m_b_e_r, in set _s_e_t___n_u_m_b_e_r, from the
       message  catalog  identified by _c_a_t_a_l_o_g, where _c_a_t_a_l_o_g is a catalog de‐
       scriptor returned from an earlier call to ccaattooppeenn(3).  The fourth argu‐
       ment, _m_e_s_s_a_g_e, points to a default message string  which  will  be  re‐
       turned  by ccaattggeettss() if the identified message catalog is not currently
       available.  The message‐text is contained in an  internal  buffer  area
       and  should  be copied by the application if it is to be saved or modi‐
       fied.  The return string is always terminated with a null byte ('\0').

